// Title: PUA - Crassus Execution
// Sigma ID: 2c32b543-1058-4808-91c6-5b31b8bed6c5
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: pH-T (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-04-17 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: discovery, reconnaissance, T1590.001
// Description: Detects Crassus, a Windows privilege escalation discovery tool, based on PE metadata
//   characteristics.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://github.com/vu-ls/Crassus
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_pua_crassus.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\Crassus.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "Crassus.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoFileDescription contains "Crassus"
